{
  "info": {
    "name": "Map Service (Team 14)",
    "description": "Geolocation updates, nearby-user queries, and proximity detection.\n\nOwner: Dackohn. Default port: 8085.\n\nEvery endpoint except /health and /docs needs a user token, sent as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Identity is the token's `sub` claim: the userId in the path or body must be that user, per the CPR's authentication contract.\n\nRun the requests top to bottom: the `Get Dev Token` requests mint a token per test user, so every later request works without copy-pasting anything. The user ids come from the service's built-in mock of User Management: u1-u3 are friends, u1-u5 are enemies, everyone else is unrelated.\n\nThe WebSocket stream endpoint cannot be stored in Postman's collection file format; see the `Live Location Stream (WebSocket)` folder for how to add it in the app.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Guard against running a request before the one that sets its variable.",
          "const url = pm.request.url.toString();",
          "const headers = JSON.stringify(pm.request.headers);",
          "const needed = [",
          "    { name: 'u1Token', setBy: 'Get Dev Token (u1)' },",
          "    { name: 'u2Token', setBy: 'Get Dev Token (u2)' },",
          "    { name: 'u3Token', setBy: 'Get Dev Token (u3)' },",
          "    { name: 'u5Token', setBy: 'Get Dev Token (u5)' },",
          "    { name: 'u6Token', setBy: 'Get Dev Token (u6)' },",
          "];",
          "",
          "needed.forEach(function (v) {",
          "    const token = '{{' + v.name + '}}';",
          "    if (url.indexOf(token) === -1 && headers.indexOf(token) === -1) return;",
          "    if (!pm.collectionVariables.get(v.name)) {",
          "        throw new Error(",
          "            'Collection variable {{' + v.name + '}} is empty. Run \"' + v.setBy +",
          "            '\" first, or use Run Collection so the requests execute in order.'",
          "        );",
          "    }",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
