      "description": "`WS {{baseUrl}}/map/stream` - continuous geolocation streaming.\n\nPostman's collection file format (v2.1) cannot store WebSocket requests, so this one has to be created inside the Postman app:\n\n1. Run `Get Dev Token (u1)` and copy the token from its response (or from the u1Token collection variable).\n2. New -> WebSocket Request\n3. URL: ws://localhost:8085/map/stream?token=<token> - WebSocket clients can't set headers, so the token goes on the URL.\n4. Connect.\n5. Send this JSON message (userId must be the token's user):\n   { \"userId\": \"u1\", \"lat\": 47.02, \"lng\": 28.83, \"timestamp\": \"<now, ISO 8601>\" }\n6. The server acks each frame:\n   { \"event\": \"ack\", \"data\": { \"status\": \"updated\" } }\n\nA missing/invalid token, or a frame for another user, closes the connection with code 1008. Sending invalid JSON gets back { \"event\": \"error\", \"data\": { \"message\": \"invalid JSON\" } }.",
      "item": []
    }
  ]
